.TH smi-external-ip "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-external-ip \- Print the external Internet IP address of this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-external-ip
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-external-ip
asks public IP echo services for the address this machine is seen from on the Internet
and prints only that address, one line, so it can be used in scripts.
.PP
The services are tried in order and the first valid answer is printed:
.IP 1. 4
.B https://icanhazip.com
.IP 2. 4
.B https://ifconfig.me
.IP 3. 4
.B https://api.ipify.org
.PP
Each request is made with
.BR curl (1)
and a 5 second time limit.
A service is skipped when it cannot be reached, answers with an HTTP error, or answers with
anything that is not an IPv4 or IPv6 address, such as the login page of a captive portal.
Whether an IPv4 or an IPv6 address is printed depends on how the machine reaches the service.
.PP
When \fIFILE\fR is given, the address is also written to it, one line.
The file is replaced through \fIFILE\fB.tmp\fR and \fBmv\fR, so a reader never sees a half written
file, and it is left untouched when no service gives an address, so it keeps the last known address.
.SH HALF PAST PLUGIN
.PP
The package ships the half past plugin
.IR /opt/setmy.info/lib/half-past/10_external-ip.sh ,
which
.BR smi-half-past-run (1)
runs from
.B setmy-info-half-past.timer
at half past every hour and one minute after boot.
It calls
.B smi-external-ip
with
.B ip.txt
in the directory
.BR smi-var-location (1)
prints, so the address is kept up to date there; the printed address also lands in the journal.
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl list-timers setmy-info-half-past.timer
journalctl -u setmy-info-half-past.service
cat /var/opt/setmy.info/ip.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/opt/setmy.info/ip.txt
External IP address written by the half past plugin.
.TP
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/half-past/10_external-ip.sh
The half past plugin.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The address was printed, and written to \fIFILE\fR when given.
.TP
.B 1
No service gave an address, or \fIFILE\fR could not be written; an error message is printed
to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
smi-external-ip
EXTERNAL_IP=$(smi-external-ip) || exit 1
smi-external-ip /var/opt/setmy.info/ip.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
